--- Splits a list into elements that satisfy a predicate and those that do not.
---
--- @details
--- `partition` takes `[pred, xs]` and returns `[matching, rest]` —
--- two lists preserving the original order: the elements for which
--- `pred(x)` is truthy, then the elements for which it is not. It is
--- the `comb`-surface spelling of `combinators.partition`.
---
--- @example
--- `[x ~> x % 2 == 0, [1, 2, 3, 4]] >>> comb.partition`
--- -- => [[2, 4], [1, 3]]
---
export partition := [pred, xs] ~> combinators.partition(pred, xs)
